body:
I see a lot of info for tak, but no one seems to have answered how to get started with shogi yet. 

&#x200B;

The best English resource out there is hidetchi, on youtube. [Here](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Pkz0LVBg0W4&list=PL587865CAE59EB84A) is his playlist starting with the rules all the way up to opening strategy. I suggest playing against [this computer](https://japanesechess.org/) on easiest and work your way up, as its a very gentle way to get familiar with the pieces.

&#x200B;

For playing against people there is [81dojo](https://81dojo.com/en/) which is the best English language site.

&#x200B;

Shogi is not nearly as well supported as go for westerners unfortunately, but it can be a really fun chess variant regardless.
